(5555399, 800636, 103142, '<td valign="top">I don''t remember if I commented or not -- what an incredible shot! I''m jealous! Very well done--a well deserved blue! (should have been higher than a 7.0, as well!)  Can you tell I really like it?</td>', 'I don''t remember if I commented or not -- what an incredible shot! I''m jealous! Very well done--a well deserved blue! (should have been higher than a 7.0, as well!)  Can you tell I really like it?', '2009-07-02 11:31:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5555459, 801313, 98339, '<td valign="top">your colors are excellent and your flag is very sharp and crisp..I gave you a 7 for this (but I am finding that I have been voting higher than most of recent)  IMO though you are lower than the top of the flag if you had gone to the base of the flag and looked up (more from the ground level) and taken a shot...I would have given you more points...those in this challenge that did just that...gave you a obvious point of view from the ground up (straight up) got higher scores from me...</td>', 'your colors are excellent and your flag is very sharp and crisp..I gave you a 7 for this (but I am finding that I have been voting higher than most of recent)  IMO though you are lower than the top of the flag if you had gone to the base of the flag and looked up (more from the ground level) and taken a shot...I would have given you more points...those in this challenge that did just that...gave you a obvious point of view from the ground up (straight up) got higher scores from me...', '2009-07-02 12:26:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5555465, 801313, 7743, '<td valign="top">The picture is very clear and sharp though I think it may have done better using the portrait orientation and exploiting the vertical aspect of the flag pole.<br/> <br/>I didn''t vote in this challenge but probably would have scored it a 5.<br/> <br/>When taking pictures of common things, try shooting from an unusual angle to add interest and dynamics to to the image.</td>', 'The picture is very clear and sharp though I think it may have done better using the portrait orientation and exploiting the vertical aspect of the flag pole. I didn''t vote in this challenge but probably would have scored it a 5. When taking pictures of common things, try shooting from an unusual angle to add interest and dynamics to to the image.', '2009-07-02 12:32:19.000000', NULL, 0),
