(5556877, 800636, 24454, '<td valign="top">Well. . .I''ve had to write this and re-write this.  At first I was so angry and hurt and felt so righteously indignant because I know I edited this legally, and I couln''t believe that a person could really lose a ribbon won fair and square when they hadn''t violated any of the editing rules. <br/> <br/>But after knowing <i>why</i> they thought I used illegal editing steps, I realized the whole thing was in fact my fault.   Not that I did anything illegal in my editing.  I didn''t.  But in my <i>explanation</i> of the steps I used, I <i>said </i>I did something I didn''t actually do.  I had already had to validate my zen photo just 2 days earlier, and I was so exhausted -- and excited and anxious -- so I hurried thru my explanation, and absent mindedly got the 2 photos mixed up and said I did a step that I had done in my zen photo that I really didn''t do in this one.  I think part of the reason I was so careless in my explanation was because this one was so easy.  I wasn''t worried in the LEAST about this one being validated and I was so tired.  So I lost a ribbon that was won fair and square because I hurried thru my explanation and typed it wrong. :(  But its not site council''s fault.  They were just going by what I said I did. <br/> <br/>This is my untouched original.  It hardly needed any editing except a little cropping, lightening and contrasting.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=803990" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/20000-24999/24454/120/803990.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/20000-24999/24454/120/803990.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/20000-24999/24454/120/803990.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-07-03 00:31:22.</i></td>', 'Well. . .I''ve had to write this and re-write this.  At first I was so angry and hurt and felt so righteously indignant because I know I edited this legally, and I couln''t believe that a person could really lose a ribbon won fair and square when they hadn''t violated any of the editing rules.  But after knowing why they thought I used illegal editing steps, I realized the whole thing was in fact my fault.   Not that I did anything illegal in my editing.  I didn''t.  But in my explanation of the steps I used, I said I did something I didn''t actually do.  I had already had to validate my zen photo just 2 days earlier, and I was so exhausted -- and excited and anxious -- so I hurried thru my explanation, and absent mindedly got the 2 photos mixed up and said I did a step that I had done in my zen photo that I really didn''t do in this one.  I think part of the reason I was so careless in my explanation was because this one was so easy.  I wasn''t worried in the LEAST about this one being validated and I was so tired.  So I lost a ribbon that was won fair and square because I hurried thru my explanation and typed it wrong. :(  But its not site council''s fault.  They were just going by what I said I did.  This is my untouched original.  It hardly needed any editing except a little cropping, lightening and contrasting.', '2009-07-02 23:02:06.000000', '2009-07-03 01:31:22.000000', 0),
